IELTS.lesson({"test": 3, "part": 1, "title": "Test 3, Part 1 — the interview", "candidate": "lama", "script": [{"who": "examiner", "text": "Good morning. Come in, have a seat.", "ar": "صباح الخير. تفضّلي بالدخول واجلسي.", "shot": "two", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/1b2def3fa2b0b362.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "My name is Mohamad Khorbatli. Can you tell me your full name, please?", "ar": "اسمي محمد خرباطلي. هل يمكنكِ أن تخبريني باسمكِ الكامل من فضلك؟", "shot": "two", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/c756d0707f344069.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "Lama Haddad.", "ar": "لمى حداد.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "f", "voice": "piper-en_US-amy-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/0d7312088795a6db.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "And what can I call you?", "ar": "وبماذا أناديكِ؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/5085ae49113e09cf.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "Lama is fine.", "ar": "لمى تكفي.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "f", "voice": "piper-en_US-amy-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/a0672b143bf95927.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Thank you, Lama. Can I see your identification, please?", "ar": "شكراً لكِ يا لمى. هل يمكنني رؤية هويتكِ من فضلك؟", "shot": "two", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/659aa2a537d88889.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "Of course. Here you are.", "ar": "بالتأكيد. تفضّل.", "shot": null, "sex": "f", "voice": "piper-en_US-amy-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/bd2e669f1f8fe87e.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Thank you. That's all fine.", "ar": "شكراً. كل شيء على ما يرام.", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/a65ff8d3eccec277.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Now, in this first part I'd like to ask you some questions about yourself. Let's talk about food and cooking.", "ar": "الآن، في هذا الجزء الأول أودّ أن أطرح عليكِ بعض الأسئلة عنكِ. لنتحدّث عن الطعام والطبخ.", "shot": "two", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/7a857cd48480d00b.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Do you enjoy cooking?", "ar": "هل تستمتعين بالطبخ؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/a64f54b60c9be37f.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "I do, though I think I'm better at feeding people than at cooking for them. I can make about six things properly, and I make all six far too often, so my mother knows exactly what's coming.", "ar": "نعم، لكنّي أظنّ أنّني أجيد إطعام الناس أكثر مما أجيد الطبخ لهم. أستطيع أن أعدّ ستة أطباق بإتقان، وأعدّ الستة جميعها أكثر من اللازم بكثير، فأمي تعرف تماماً ما الذي سيأتي.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "f", "voice": "piper-en_US-amy-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/cf3974c5379ee00a.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Who usually cooks in your home?", "ar": "من يطبخ عادةً في بيتكم؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/cd61b51a7817806a.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "My mother, and she'd say that's because nobody else can, which isn't quite fair but isn't entirely unfair either. Mind you, she's never actually let anyone try for long enough to find out.", "ar": "أمي، وهي ستقول إنّ السبب أنّ لا أحد غيرها يستطيع، وهذا ليس منصفاً تماماً لكنّه ليس ظالماً تماماً أيضاً. على فكرة، هي لم تترك أحداً يحاول مدّة كافية ليعرف.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "f", "voice": "piper-en_US-amy-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/162813faba1549f5.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Has the food you eat changed since you were a child?", "ar": "هل تغيّر الطعام الذي تأكلينه منذ كنتِ طفلة؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/62006455c23b62d7.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "Less than it should have, I think. The one real change is that we eat later. In Damascus everything moved when the evenings became the only reliable part of the day, and a meal at ten at night isn't the same meal even when it's the same food.", "ar": "أقلّ مما كان يجب، كما أظنّ. التغيير الحقيقي الوحيد أنّنا نأكل في وقت متأخّر. في دمشق تحرّك كلّ شيء حين صار المساء الجزء الوحيد الذي يمكن الاعتماد عليه من اليوم، ووجبة في العاشرة ليلاً ليست الوجبة نفسها حتى لو كان الطعام نفسه.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "f", "voice": "piper-en_US-amy-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/dd7561593e162138.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Is there any food you really dislike?", "ar": "هل هناك طعام لا تحبّينه فعلاً؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/9f97bc7f4cbad792.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "Aubergine, which in Syria is almost something you have to admit to. It's in everything, actually. I've spent my whole life quietly moving it to the side of the plate, and I don't think anyone has ever noticed.", "ar": "الباذنجان، وهذا في سوريا يكاد يكون اعترافاً. إنّه في كلّ شيء، في الحقيقة. قضيت عمري كلّه أزيحه بهدوء إلى طرف الصحن، ولا أظنّ أنّ أحداً لاحظ ذلك يوماً.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "f", "voice": "piper-en_US-amy-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/f19e206948882f9d.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Let's move on to talk about weekends.", "ar": "لننتقل للحديث عن عطلة نهاية الأسبوع.", "shot": "two", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/f77b9ebd307852a5.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "What do you usually do at the weekend?", "ar": "ماذا تفعلين عادةً في عطلة نهاية الأسبوع؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/98960ced90472fdb.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "Friday is my grandmother's, and of course that isn't negotiable. Everyone goes, lunch is at two and nobody leaves before five, and I've stopped pretending I have a say in it. Saturday I catch up on everything Friday cost me.", "ar": "الجمعة لجدّتي، وهذا طبعاً غير قابل للنقاش. الجميع يذهب، والغداء في الثانية ولا أحد يغادر قبل الخامسة، وقد كففت عن التظاهر بأنّ لي رأياً في الأمر. أمّا السبت فأعوّض فيه كلّ ما كلّفتني إيّاه الجمعة.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "f", "voice": "piper-en_US-amy-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/2158c8637f22c1a9.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Do you prefer to spend the weekend at home or going out?", "ar": "هل تفضّلين قضاء العطلة في البيت أم الخروج؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/83e5096b3a6a04fc.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "At home, at the moment. I keep checking whether that's what I actually want or whether the hospital has just worn me out, and I think it's the first one. Ask me again after exams and you might get a different answer.", "ar": "في البيت، في هذه الفترة. أظلّ أسأل نفسي إن كان هذا ما أريده فعلاً أم أنّ المشفى أنهكني فحسب، وأظنّ أنّه الأوّل. اسألني مرّة أخرى بعد الامتحانات وقد تحصل على جواب مختلف.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "f", "voice": "piper-en_US-amy-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/811346b701e0ffff.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Are weekends different now from when you were a child?", "ar": "هل تختلف عطلة نهاية الأسبوع الآن عمّا كانت حين كنتِ طفلة؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/a92d5b6e27f1b37d.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "Much quieter, mainly because the family's smaller than it was. The same Friday lunch happens in the same room with about half the people, and nobody ever mentions it. I think that's harder than if they did.", "ar": "أهدأ بكثير، وذلك أساساً لأنّ العائلة صارت أصغر مما كانت. غداء الجمعة نفسه يحدث في الغرفة نفسها مع نصف العدد تقريباً، ولا أحد يذكر ذلك أبداً. أظنّ أنّ هذا أصعب من لو أنّهم ذكروه.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "f", "voice": "piper-en_US-amy-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/eba4f1660bf56142.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Do you think people should work at the weekend?", "ar": "هل تظنّين أنّ على الناس أن يعملوا في عطلة نهاية الأسبوع؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/e9498095dd972496.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "If the work genuinely needs it, then of course yes. What I'd argue with is the assumption that it does. Half the weekend work I see at the hospital exists because somebody didn't plan Wednesday properly. That isn't an emergency. It's a habit.", "ar": "إذا كان العمل يحتاج ذلك فعلاً، فنعم بالتأكيد. ما أعترض عليه هو افتراض أنّه يحتاج ذلك. نصف عمل العطلة الذي أراه في المشفى موجود لأنّ أحدهم لم يخطّط ليوم الأربعاء كما يجب. هذه ليست حالة طارئة. هذه عادة.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "f", "voice": "piper-en_US-amy-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/61bb112640d84812.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Finally in this part, let's talk about photographs.", "ar": "وأخيراً في هذا الجزء، لنتحدّث عن الصور.", "shot": "two", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/1b8ae0806744c3bd.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Do you take many photographs?", "ar": "هل تلتقطين صوراً كثيرة؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/8feedc01cc8e57e3.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "Far too many, and I don't look at any of them, which I think is normal now. There are about four thousand of them on my phone. There's maybe nine I could describe, and most of those are from one Friday lunch.", "ar": "كثيرة جداً، ولا أنظر إلى أيّ منها، وأظنّ أنّ هذا صار أمراً عادياً. هناك نحو أربعة آلاف صورة على هاتفي. ربّما تسع منها أستطيع أن أصفها، ومعظمها من غداء جمعة واحد.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "f", "voice": "piper-en_US-amy-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/2850dcfbd6e0ca85.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Do you prefer taking photos of people or places?", "ar": "هل تفضّلين تصوير الأشخاص أم الأماكن؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/1041184b8cc70094.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "People, although I'm honestly bad at it, because I always wait until everyone is ready and the ready ones are never the good ones. The photographs I keep are all of people at Friday lunch who hadn't noticed me.", "ar": "الأشخاص، مع أنّني سيّئة في ذلك بصراحة، لأنّني أنتظر دائماً حتى يصبح الجميع مستعدّين، والصور المستعدّة ليست الجيّدة أبداً. الصور التي أحتفظ بها كلّها لأشخاص في غداء الجمعة لم ينتبهوا إليّ.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "f", "voice": "piper-en_US-amy-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/e8b45107ac5ba095.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Do you ever print your photographs?", "ar": "هل تطبعين صورك أحياناً؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/b24ce671323dd55f.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "Almost never, and I think my grandmother finds that genuinely upsetting. She's got an album with the dates written underneath in pencil, and mine only exist on a phone, which she doesn't really count as existing.", "ar": "لا أفعل تقريباً، وأظنّ أنّ جدّتي تجد ذلك محزناً فعلاً. عندها ألبوم والتواريخ مكتوبة تحت الصور بالقلم الرصاص، أمّا صوري فموجودة على الهاتف فقط، وهي لا تعدّ ذلك وجوداً حقيقياً.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "f", "voice": "piper-en_US-amy-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/4a1c4690dd702ea0.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Why do you think people like looking at old photographs?", "ar": "لماذا تظنّين أنّ الناس يحبّون النظر إلى الصور القديمة؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/2a96f2b81926c309.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "I think it's about proof more than memory. A photograph shows that the version of you who existed then really did exist, and nobody needs that until they're old enough to start doubting it. My grandmother's album is mostly that.", "ar": "أظنّ أنّ الأمر يتعلّق بالإثبات أكثر من الذكرى. الصورة تُظهر أنّ النسخة منكِ التي كانت موجودة حينها كانت موجودة فعلاً، ولا أحد يحتاج ذلك حتى يكبر بما يكفي ليبدأ بالشكّ فيه. ألبوم جدّتي هو هذا في معظمه.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "f", "voice": "piper-en_US-amy-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/d3b0cd298a0eab94.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Thank you. That is the end of Part One.", "ar": "شكراً لكِ. بهذا ينتهي القسم الأول.", "shot": "two", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/50f379466faf1658.mp3"}], "boxes": [{"q": "Do you enjoy cooking?", "ar": null, "topic": "Food and cooking", "model": "I do, though I think I'm better at feeding people than at cooking for them. I can make about six things properly, and I make all six far too often, so my mother knows exactly what's coming.", "why": "A comparison instead of a declared distinction, and the self-deprecation carries a number. The mother in the last clause keeps the answer from being only about the speaker."}, {"q": "Who usually cooks in your home?", "ar": null, "topic": "Food and cooking", "model": "My mother, and she'd say that's because nobody else can, which isn't quite fair but isn't entirely unfair either. Mind you, she's never actually let anyone try for long enough to find out.", "why": "Reported speech, a double hedge, then a turn. 'Mind you' is Lama's marker and it is being used precisely — to add a qualifying aside."}, {"q": "Has the food you eat changed since you were a child?", "ar": null, "topic": "Food and cooking", "model": "Less than it should have, I think. The one real change is that we eat later. In Damascus everything moved when the evenings became the only reliable part of the day, and a meal at ten at night isn't the same meal even when it's the same food.", "why": "A durable observation about daily life that dates nothing. The insight is the last sentence and it is said in one breath."}, {"q": "Is there any food you really dislike?", "ar": null, "topic": "Food and cooking", "model": "Aubergine, which in Syria is almost something you have to admit to. It's in everything, actually. I've spent my whole life quietly moving it to the side of the plate, and I don't think anyone has ever noticed.", "why": "A specific with a cultural gloss, a present perfect with a duration, and a landing that is funny without being a joke."}, {"q": "What do you usually do at the weekend?", "ar": null, "topic": "Weekends", "model": "Friday is my grandmother's, and of course that isn't negotiable. Everyone goes, lunch is at two and nobody leaves before five, and I've stopped pretending I have a say in it. Saturday I catch up on everything Friday cost me.", "why": "Two days, two registers. 'Of course that isn't negotiable' is a marker doing real work."}, {"q": "Do you prefer to spend the weekend at home or going out?", "ar": null, "topic": "Weekends", "model": "At home, at the moment. I keep checking whether that's what I actually want or whether the hospital has just worn me out, and I think it's the first one. Ask me again after exams and you might get a different answer.", "why": "Self-examination rather than a preference, said as a person says it: a question she is still checking, and an answer she will not swear to."}, {"q": "Are weekends different now from when you were a child?", "ar": null, "topic": "Weekends", "model": "Much quieter, mainly because the family's smaller than it was. The same Friday lunch happens in the same room with about half the people, and nobody ever mentions it. I think that's harder than if they did.", "why": "Handles loss in one clause and moves on. 'Harder than if they did' is a comparative built on the fly."}, {"q": "Do you think people should work at the weekend?", "ar": null, "topic": "Weekends", "model": "If the work genuinely needs it, then of course yes. What I'd argue with is the assumption that it does. Half the weekend work I see at the hospital exists because somebody didn't plan Wednesday properly. That isn't an emergency. It's a habit.", "why": "Conditional, concession, then a sharp distinction with evidence behind it. This is Part 3 quality arriving in Part 1."}, {"q": "Do you take many photographs?", "ar": null, "topic": "Photographs", "model": "Far too many, and I don't look at any of them, which I think is normal now. There are about four thousand of them on my phone. There's maybe nine I could describe, and most of those are from one Friday lunch.", "why": "A generalisation checked against a number. Four thousand against nine is the whole answer, and the Friday lunch stops it being about anybody's phone."}, {"q": "Do you prefer taking photos of people or places?", "ar": null, "topic": "Photographs", "model": "People, although I'm honestly bad at it, because I always wait until everyone is ready and the ready ones are never the good ones. The photographs I keep are all of people at Friday lunch who hadn't noticed me.", "why": "Admits a fault and turns it into an observation. 'The ready ones are never the good ones' is an aphorism she builds while speaking."}, {"q": "Do you ever print your photographs?", "ar": null, "topic": "Photographs", "model": "Almost never, and I think my grandmother finds that genuinely upsetting. She's got an album with the dates written underneath in pencil, and mine only exist on a phone, which she doesn't really count as existing.", "why": "A second person's view doubles the material. 'Which she doesn't really count as existing' is precise and slightly funny."}, {"q": "Why do you think people like looking at old photographs?", "ar": null, "topic": "Photographs", "model": "I think it's about proof more than memory. A photograph shows that the version of you who existed then really did exist, and nobody needs that until they're old enough to start doubting it. My grandmother's album is mostly that.", "why": "Reframes the question, then supplies a reason that is hers rather than general."}], "voices": {"examiner": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "candidate": "piper-en_US-amy-medium-s119"}});
